3
00:00:08.991 --> 00:00:14.182
Start from last year's: the same costs
come across, and so does the month the

4
00:00:14.182 --> 00:00:15.682
year starts.

5
00:00:17.275 --> 00:00:19.775
Add what's new this year — here, a lift
servicing contract — and save.

6
00:00:27.616 --> 00:00:31.885
The total is split by floor area: each
unit's share of the budget, and the

7
00:00:31.885 --> 00:00:33.616
monthly charge that covers it.

8
00:00:34.751 --> 00:00:38.751
Amber means the tenant pays less than
their share today.

9
00:00:41.694 --> 00:00:46.700
Apply to tenants sets everyone's monthly
service charge to match, from their next

10
00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.200
invoice.

11
00:00:53.089 --> 00:00:58.262
Budget vs actual tracks what's been spent
against the budget, cost by cost, all

12
00:00:58.262 --> 00:00:59.762
year.

13
00:01:02.108 --> 00:01:07.220
When the year ends, each tenant's share of
what was actually spent is set against

14
00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:08.720
what they were billed.

15
00:01:09.746 --> 00:01:13.246
Days a unit stood empty are the owner's
share.

16
00:01:15.527 --> 00:01:20.882
Shortfalls become draft balancing invoices
in one click. Credits are listed for you

17
00:01:20.882 --> 00:01:22.382
